invariant: INV-14
file: quic_token.c
catches: srv_quic_test
reason: the check compares the token's tag with itself rather than with the
  tag the key computes, so every Retry token of the right length checks and
  a client forges one for any address with no key at all. The tamper sweep
  in test/quic_token_tests.h flips each tag byte and requires a refusal,
  and the other-key and other-address cases require one too.

--- old
    uint32_t equal = ct_memeq(tag, want, SHA256_LEN);
--- new
    uint32_t equal = ct_memeq(tag, tag, SHA256_LEN);
